# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules

# Build output. Cloudflare Pages builds from source on every push, so the bundle
# is never committed — a committed bundle only ever goes stale and bloats clones.
#
# `docs` used to be listed here too, copied in from the GitHub Pages convention
# where a site builds into docs/. Nothing in this repo does: vite.config.ts sets
# outDir to `dist`. All the rule ever did was silently swallow written
# documentation, which is the opposite of what a build-output ignore is for.
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Local editor/tooling config.
.claude/

# Secrets. This app talks to OpenRouter directly from the browser, so a key that
# lands in the tree can also get baked into a committed bundle. The patterns
# below cover more than this repo currently needs on purpose: it is AGPL, people
# will fork it, and the cost of a too-wide ignore rule is nothing next to the
# cost of a forked repo committing its own key.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
secrets.json
credentials.json
.npmrc

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
